F2FS legacy project quota compatibility test
===========================================

Build with:
  make -C tools/testing/selftests TARGETS=filesystems/f2fs

Run only inside an isolated VM with two fresh, disposable F2FS images mounted
at separate mountpoints. The first image must lack project_quota; the second
must have extra_attr, project_quota and quota. Neither image should enable
compression. The runner does not format devices and is skipped unless opted in:

  F2FS_COMPAT_TEST=1 ./run.sh /mnt/legacy /mnt/native

The runner creates scratch directories and changes mount options. It leaves
those directories behind, returns both filesystems to read/write mode, and
disables legacy compatibility on the legacy mount. Use fresh images per run.
Do not point it at userdata, application directories, or production volumes.

Coverage includes strict rejection, mount-specific opt-in, honest project ID
and inheritance readback, child inheritance, preservation of unrelated flags
and errors, owner/non-owner permission boundaries, regular-file exclusion,
read-only rejection, and successful/failed remount stress. Stress tests alone
cannot prove freedom from remount races; the implementation snapshots a policy
published only after successful mount/remount completion.

The ioctl utility also supports verify-compat and verify-native modes, for
checking the test directory after a complete unmount/mount or VM reboot:

  ./project_quota_compat /mnt/legacy/f2fs-compat-test/compat verify-compat
  ./project_quota_compat /mnt/native/f2fs-compat-test/native verify-native

Expected legacy readback is project ID 0 with no inheritance flag. Expected
native readback is project ID 12345 with inheritance enabled. This fallback
does not implement project accounting or limits on a legacy filesystem.
